<title>SPAIN: Fenosa says '96 financial costs down 18 pct.</title>
<headline>Fenosa says '96 financial costs down 18 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish electricity firm Union Fenosa said on Wednesday that financial costs in the year to 1996 fell 18.1 percent to 43.03 billion pesetas from 52.54 billion pesetas in 1995.</p>
<p>The firm said this reduction was mainly due to a fall in debt of more than 27 billion pesetas, and a reduction in the cost of debt thanks to lower interest rates.</p>
<p>Union Fenosa expects to release results today.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
